Subject: [PATCH] winex11: Wait for the PRIME offload frame before copying offscreen GL.

On hybrid laptops the NVIDIA driver renders with PRIME render offload: after a swap it
hands the finished frame to the X server from its own X connection, asynchronously. Wine
copies the offscreen drawable of a child window (After Effects' composition viewer) into
the toplevel right after the swap, over gdi_display, so the copy often overtook the
driver and read the previous frame. glFinish (0007) only waits for the GPU, not for the
driver's hand-off.

Measured with a GL child window presenting a new colour at 30 fps and reading the screen
back 25 ms later: 4-20 of 90 frames never reached the screen (they showed the previous
colour until the next frame); with the Intel GPU, or with a 1 ms pause after the swap,
none did. In After Effects the viewer of a moving-layer comp went from 22 to 27 updates
per second (30 fps comp; 27 is also what the Intel GPU reaches) and long playhead stalls
dropped from 48 to 19 in 25 s.

Pause 2 ms after glFinish/XFlush on this path (offscreen drawable, no
GLX_OML_sync_control). Applied to the Proton-CachyOS 11.0 build as a binary patch by
lib/patch_runner.py.
---
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/opengl.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/opengl.c
@@ -1483,12 +1483,17 @@
         if (pglXWaitForSbcOML) pglXWaitForSbcOML( gdi_display, gl->drawable, target_sbc, &ust, &msc, &sbc );
     }
 
     if (offscreen && !pglXWaitForSbcOML)
     {
         /* no GLX_OML_sync_control (NVIDIA): make sure the swap is done before the copy */
         funcs->p_glFinish();
         XFlush( gdi_display );
+        /* PRIME render offload delivers the frame to the X server from the driver's own
+         * connection; give it a moment, or the copy below reads the previous frame */
+        poll( NULL, 0, 2 );
     }
 
     client_surface_present( base->client );
     return TRUE;
